{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SpinWait.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SpinWait.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"spin wait spin wait","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SpinWait.md","fileName":"SpinWait.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SpinWait","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 00:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Synchronization and Thread Coordination]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Synchronization and Thread Coordination","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SpinWait.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SpinWait.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"spin wait spin wait","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SpinWait.md","fileName":"SpinWait.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SpinWait","heading":"SpinWait","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"`SpinWait` provides a progressive spinning strategy for very short waits. Repeated calls initially use processor-level spinning and can later yield so that a waiting loop does not monopolize the current execution time indefinitely.\n\nIt is a low-level building block, not a substitute for a condition variable or asynchronous wait. The expected wait must be short, and the loop must read state with the memory-order guarantees required to observe another thread's update.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Synchronization and Thread Coordination","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/SpinWait.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/SpinWait.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"spin wait spin wait","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/SpinWait.md","fileName":"SpinWait.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"SpinWait","heading":"References",